---
import DocLayout from "../../layouts/DocLayout.astro";
import { withBase } from "../../data/nav";
---

<DocLayout title="Docs" description="Tangled protocol specification: Solana identity, signed Merkle repos, capability ACL, sealed records.">
  <p class="callout">
    This site is a specification, not a running network. There is no public graph to join.
  </p>
  <h1>Tangled specification</h1>
  <p>
    A content-network protocol. Identity is a Solana Ed25519 public key. Content lives in a signed Merkle
    repository on a host the identity controls (a <strong>knot</strong>). Authorization is object-capability.
    Confidentiality is encryption. Discovery and moderation are unprivileged overlays.
  </p>
  <div class="claims">
    <div class="claim">
      <strong>One data plane</strong>
      <span>Public, capability-gated, and sealed records share one repository and one sync protocol. Visibility is a field.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="claim">
      <strong>Self-host is the unit</strong>
      <span>One process and a local database is enough to exist. Looms are optional indexes of public heads.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="claim">
      <strong>Fetch ≠ read</strong>
      <span>Capabilities gate who a knot serves. Hybrid Public Key Encryption (HPKE) and Messaging Layer Security (MLS) gate who can decrypt. Circles never show those names to users.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="claim">
      <strong>Other networks bind in</strong>
      <span>Nostr, AT Protocol, ActivityPub, and Farcaster identities bind with provenance. ActivityPub imports are host-attested.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <h2 id="architecture">Architecture</h2>
  <pre class="sig-line">{`Wallet ──sign──► Knot (repo MST + blobs)
                    ▲
                    │ Merkle pull
                 Knot B     Loom (optional public index)
                                Gateway ──► AP / Nostr / AT Protocol`}</pre>
  <p>
    Followers pull. Authors do not POST into N inboxes. Relays are not the source of truth. The source of truth is a signed commit.
  </p>
  <p>
    Start at the <a href={withBase("/spec/abstract")}>abstract</a>, the <a href={withBase("/terminology")}>terminology</a> page (every acronym), the
    <a href={withBase("/spec/use-cases")}>use cases</a>, or the <a href={withBase("/reference/types")}>type index</a>.
  </p>
</DocLayout>
